  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Hashti, in most traditional houses in Iran, is a octagonal space of distribution and circulation to direct the person towards the various parts of the house, the private (andarouni) and semi-public (birouni) reserved for the reception from abroad and the access to spaces of service. Hashti Tehran is a film and discursive project initiated by filmmaker Daniel Kötter in collaboration with environmentalist Shadnaz Azizi, architect and urban designer Kaveh Rashidzadeh, urban planner Pouya Sepehr and sociologist Amir Tehrani"-- Publisher's website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
